# handle-chat-sdk enclave. Exact repo-root-relative paths; no wildcards, no directory prefixes.
# A PR touching any of these that merges into master needs operator approval. Why each is here: CANONICAL_CONTRACT.md.
# The SDK holds no crypto of its own; it republishes chat.handle.me's client core. What matters here is
# what gets published to npm and that the cross-repo identity vector never changes.
.enclave
CANONICAL_CONTRACT.md

# publishing: a push to master publishes the public npm package
.github/workflows/deploy.yml
package.json
.npmrc

# what is compiled and exported, and from where
scripts/build.mjs
sdk/index.ts

# the cross-repo identity vector and the guardian codec contract
test/sdk.test.mjs
